"Supplementary Table 16. Results from DEPICT gene prioritization analysis. Within each height-associated locus, genes were prioritized using the Data-driven Enrichment-Prioritized Integration for Complex Traits (DEPICT) method. Locus gene sets were constructed by mapping genes to a given locus if they were within, or overlapped with, regions defined by linkage disequilibrium r2>0.5 around the lead SNP of that locus. The DEPICT method prioritizes genes within a given associated loci based on the genes’ functional similarity to genes from other height-associated loci. Genes that are highly similar to genes from other loci obtain low prioritization P-values. Prioritization P-values are adjusted for the number of genes in the given and significance was set at FDR<0.05. Table lists also the biological evidence for each prioritized gene: 1) DEPICT gene set evidence (Supplementary Table 14); 2) OMIM evidence (Supplementary Table 9); 3) GRAIL evidence (Supplementary Table 13); 4) and 5) rodent growth plate evidence&; 6) Jackson Lab evidence was obtained by matching Gene column entries to Jackson Lab database (http://www.informatics.jax.org/) on genes reported to have either ""growth/size"", ""limb/tail/digit"" or ""skeleton"" phenotype; 7) eQTL evidence#; 8) nsSNP evidence (Supplementary Table 7) and 9) distance evidence (Supplementary Table 1). Only genes that were significantly prioritized (FDR<0.05) are listed.

#eQTL lists obtained from Westra et al. 2013 (ref. 21)
